---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/wiki/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Base layout="full" title="Privacy" description="How The Ledger uses anonymous product analytics.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="§ About the Ledger" title="Privacy" subtitle="What we collect when you read the archive." />

  <article class="prose privacy-prose">
    <h2>Anonymous product analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PostHog</a>
      to understand how readers use the archive.
      Analytics includes page views, page paths and referring sites, browser and device information,
      and actions such as opening sources, choosing filters, and search result counts.
      We do not create identified reader profiles.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not send search text or input values, record sessions, or collect heatmaps.
      Query strings and fragments are removed from URLs in analytics events.
      Analytics uses memory only, with no analytics cookies, local storage, or session storage.
      The anonymous identifier resets when a new page loads.
    </p>
    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      PostHog processes the analytics events.
      Like other network requests, these requests expose your IP address to the provider.
      The site is hosted by Vercel; hosting requests are separate from product analytics.
      For a privacy question or correction, <a href="https://github.com/pedro-bright/the-ledger/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open an issue</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-prose {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
